joining us now is cbs news political  analyst and kenosha native reince  priebus who traveled to wisconsin with  the president  he previously served as the president's  white house chief of staff as well also  with us cbs news political contributor  joel payne  he is the former director of  african-american advertising for hillary  clinton's presidential campaign good  morning to both of you  uh ryan i want to start with you because  you're exactly the person to talk to  this morning  because you're a kenosha native and not  too long ago you were calling for the  renewal of the republican party by  broadening the base reaching out to  minority voters  the president yesterday seemed committed  to a very different strategy he only  visited sites of destruction he praised  law enforcement  he did not acknowledge systemic racism  has he given up  on trying to broaden his appeal  well first of all you're right i'm from  kenosha spent my entire life  in kenosha my parents live in kenosha  i think yesterday was really for kenosha  itself  more of a thank you  for freeing and saving the city  of kenosha and i can tell you it's not  spin  people were very afraid in kenosha  businesses were burned down  people were locking their doors in their  houses putting kids in basements getting  their hunting rifles out because they  were scared for their life  and i think that while many of the  things you're seeing  are important and i'm happy to get to  those i think you're  missing in your intro and the seven  o'clock hour your intro here  you are missing and dismissing the fear  that people have in this country for  wild  violence put on by people who are coming  out of town  destroying cities and businesses and it  needs to be addressed  first mr president and do do things like  that jacob blake shooting need  address absolutely but you can do both  things  you can address the issues i agree you  can do both things that is exactly and  you can  make it right doing your setup president  is ridiculous this has nothing to do  with broadening  the base of the republican party yes the  republican party needs to add they need  to multiply  they can't subtract people out of the  room and they need to talk to people of  all races  all backgrounds and talk about the  issues that matter in america well  mr priebus you can do both things and my  question pertains to why the president  has not been doing both things he's  talking only to one side of this issue  and not acknowledging the grievances of  the many thousands of peaceful people in  the streets not only in kenosha  but in cities all across the country i  want to bring in joel right now to get  his reaction  uh to what you've just said ryan and  also to talk about  uh the president's strategy overall  versus joe bidens joel what do you think  well i think tony i think your lead in  makes sense  i do think the president needs to be  talking to both sides i think that's  what the moment calls for right  it's presidential leadership and we  actually see that  the strategy that the president and his  allies have been trying to  deploy here which is to make this about  violence when we know  that violence is down across the nation  it's up in some cities but it's down  broadly  across the nation it's not working um  national polls have come out today have  shown that  the president did not get any bounce  from the rnc where they talked about  this issue ad nauseam  and i think um the president is  misplaying his hand because  what he's thinking is that this is a  suburban strategy where you're gonna  you're gonna scare people in the suburbs  so it actually what it's doing it's  backfiring  because many of those people in the  suburbs don't like it when the president  talks about race because they don't  trust him  on this issue of race and unity and  bringing people together  reince it's true what you're saying in  terms of people were very glad to see  him yesterday there  i saw the crowds lined up cheering the  president on as he drove by but  this is the thing that is so hard for  people to take  everybody agrees that the looting the  violence nobody on either side likes  that  but it seems that the president only  denounces it when it is against  him he doesn't he he doesn't seem to  embrace the violence on both sides and i  think  that's what many people are struggling  with so i'm wondering how do you address  it he condemned the protesters as thugs  but on the other side when he was asked  about kyle uh runs from the the young  man with the  with the weapon house written house  when he was asked about that he seemed  to be giving him a pass and i think  that's why it's so difficult because he  seems to be sending  mixed messages do you disagree with that  premise  i i think you know look well first of  all there's a lot of things you said  there gail first of all i think he's  very focused on portland i  you know i don't think anyone thinks  he's he's politically  going to do much in oregon but he's very  fixed on portland he wants the people in  portland  to do what the people in kenosha and  wisconsin did  by asking for help and having people  work together so i i do think it's  across the board  i've never seen anything in my life i've  been doing politics and kenosha since i  was 16.  i've never seen the city of kenosha  which is  65 percent democrat lying the streets 99  of the people saying thank you i'm sure  a lot of democrats are out there too  but i do think he addresses it in his  way when he says look  i know that there are bad apples in the  police force am i willing to say  that there is a systematic  across-the-board  racism within our police i think that's  a that's a road to fire  the last thing i'd say is even on cbs  this morning you had the attorney  general  of wisconsin on your air and he wouldn't  condemn the police because he's got an  ongoing  investigation to find out what in the  world happened how could it be possible  for a police officer to shoot someone in  the back seven times  i mean the clip itself seems impossible  to accept but at the same time they have  to do an investigation  i don't know if there's some wild piece  of evidence here that might  make this this makes sense but it's  horrific  i don't think it does make sense but i  also believe that we  need an investigation to take place so  we can see exactly what happened  i do think there are issues in in  policing that need to be addressed the  the sheriff yesterday  and the police chief one republican i  don't know what the police chief is  they both said on the first question we  need to have body cameras here  in wisconsin we need to have body  cameras in kenosha so they're moving  forward with that  joel how do we advance the conversation  when  people can't acknowledge that there  seems to be systemic racism and and i  i think right all you have to do is look  at the numbers the numbers of  black people who are killed by police  compared to the number of white people  that are killed by police  clearly there's a problem and it's  always reduced to there are just a few  bad apples  we nobody wants any bad apples and  people want  justice they want people and when when  it does happen they want  police to be held accountable and  heretofore that does not seem to be the  case and i think that's why it's so  frustrating but joel i want you to pick  up  the question about systemic racism  because  the two sides are so far apart obviously  yeah obviously there's there's systemic  racism and i think the president is  holding on to this talking point of not  wanting to acknowledge that  because he knows that law and order that  police that support for the police  across the board  is an important issue to his base and i  think he doesn't want to  harm his political base but what he is  not realizing is that the moment calls  for  presidential leadership which  occasionally calls for you  to talk to your supporters about  changing their attitudes  and the president has not shown that he  has the ability to do this  and by the way he has tried to push joe  biden into a place that he's  uncomfortable and actually think that  backfired because  we saw joe biden very forcefully talk  about the looters and the protesters  uh rather the looters and the violent  protesters being wrong but also  addressing those systemic issues there  so joe biden is showing you can do both  donald trump has no interest in doing  both yeah all right reince priebus and  joel payne thank you both very much very  interesting conversation
 

